{"etape": 8, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-27T13:20:20.521516Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "Your account balances are:\n\n- **Gift cards total:** **$327**\n  - $198\n  - $129\n\n- **Certificates total:** **$1,000**\n  - $500\n  - $250\n  - $250\n\nI found your reservation **K1NW8N**: JFK → SFO round trip, **3 passengers**, currently **basic economy**, paid **$567**.\n\nThe **cheapest business round-trip option on the same dates** is:\n\n- **May 26:** JFK → SFO, **HAT023**, business: **$364**\n- **May 28:** SFO → SEA, **HAT204**, business: **$248**\n- **May 28:** SEA → JFK, **HAT100**, business: **$259**\n\nTotal: **$871 per passenger**, or **$2,613 for 3 passengers**.\n\nHowever, your current reservation is **basic economy**, and **basic economy flights cannot be modified to different flights**. I can either:\n\n1. **Change cabin only to business while keeping the current flights**  \n   - Current business total: **$3,195**\n   - Additional cost: **$2,628**\n\n2. **Cancel the reservation and rebook the cheapest business itinerary**  \n   - Cancellation is eligible because it was booked within the last 24 hours.\n   - Refund: **$567** to the original payment method.\n   - New booking total: **$2,613**.\n\nPlease tell me which option you want, and if you want to proceed, confirm **yes** and provide the payment method(s) to use."}, "resultat": "Thank you for the detailed information.\n\nSince basic economy cannot be changed, I'd like to cancel the current reservation and book the new, cheapest business itinerary you found for $2,613.\n\nFor payment, I'd like to use my certificates as much as possible, then my gift cards as much as possible, and cover the rest with my Mastercard. Could you please tell me how much my Mastercard will be charged in this scenario? I don't need baggage or insurance. I want to minimize the Mastercard payment, so if cancelling and booking a new one costs less for the Mastercard, I will do it.", "erreur": null}
{"etape": 9, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-27T13:21:35.440620Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "Based on your **current available balances**, the Mastercard charge would be:\n\n- New business itinerary total: **$2,613**\n- Largest usable certificate: **$500**  \n  - Only **one certificate** can be used per reservation.\n- Gift cards: **$198 + $129 = $327**\n- Remaining Mastercard charge: **$1,786**\n\nThe cancellation refund for reservation **K1NW8N** is **$567**, returned to the original gift card within **5–7 business days**. If that refund were available immediately, the Mastercard charge could be reduced to **$1,219**, but it cannot be counted on for an immediate booking.\n\nCompared with changing the cabin on the existing reservation, **canceling and rebooking now is lower for the Mastercard**.\n\nPlease confirm **yes** to proceed with:\n\n1. **Cancel reservation K1NW8N**  \n   - Reason: change of plan  \n   - Refund: **$567** to original gift card\n\n2. **Book new business round trip**  \n   - JFK → SFO: **HAT023**, 2024-05-26  \n   - SFO → SEA: **HAT204**, 2024-05-28  \n   - SEA → JFK: **HAT100**, 2024-05-28  \n   - Passengers: Mohamed Silva, Raj Sanchez, Liam Wilson  \n   - Baggage: **0**  \n   - Insurance: **no**  \n   - Payment: **$500 certificate + $198 gift card + $129 gift card + $1,786 Mastercard**"}, "resultat": "I understand that only one certificate can be used per reservation, but I have an idea. Since I have three certificates, could we book three separate reservations instead?\n\nI'd like to use the $500 certificate and all gift cards for my reservation. Then, I'd like to use certificate_9984806 for Aarav's reservation, and the other certificate for Evelyn's reservation. We can then pay the remaining balance for each with my Mastercard.\n\nCould you please calculate the total Mastercard charge if we proceed this way?", "erreur": null}
{"etape": 10, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-27T13:22:21.537703Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "Yes—splitting into three separate one-passenger reservations would reduce the Mastercard charge.\n\nFor the new business itinerary, each passenger costs **$871**:\n\n- HAT023 JFK → SFO: **$364**\n- HAT204 SFO → SEA: **$248**\n- HAT100 SEA → JFK: **$259**\n\nUsing your current available balances:\n\n1. **Your reservation**\n   - Certificate: **$500**\n   - Gift cards: **$198 + $129 = $327**\n   - Mastercard: **$44**\n\n2. **Aarav’s reservation**\n   - Certificate: **$250**\n   - Mastercard: **$621**\n\n3. **Evelyn’s reservation**\n   - Certificate: **$250**\n   - Mastercard: **$621**\n\n**Total Mastercard charge: $1,286**\n\nThe cancellation refund of **$567** would go back to the original gift card within **5–7 business days**, so it cannot be used immediately for the new bookings.\n\nTo proceed, I need:\n\n- **Aarav’s full name and date of birth**\n- **Evelyn’s full name and date of birth**\n\nThen please confirm **yes** to:\n\n1. Cancel reservation **K1NW8N**\n2. Create three separate business round-trip reservations with the payment split above\n3. **0 baggage** and **no insurance**"}, "resultat": "That sounds like a great plan!\n\nAarav's full name is Aarav Sharma, and his date of birth is April 12, 1995.\nEvelyn's full name is Evelyn Chen, and her date of birth is September 23, 1998.\n\nYes, I confirm to:\n1. Cancel reservation K1NW8N.\n2. Create three separate business round-trip reservations with the payment split you outlined.\n3. 0 baggage and no insurance for all reservations.\n\nSo, just to confirm, the total Mastercard charge will be $1,286, correct?", "erreur": null}
